{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 400,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A portion of this video was sponsored by loda"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 4000,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is like a scientist trap."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 6240,
    "dDurationMs": 4600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It certainly is; case in point, that is Space Station commander Chris Hadfield"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 17000,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What this isn't is turbulent. Nope, this is largely laminar flow."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 22920,
    "dDurationMs": 1640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "“Did somebody say peculiar flow! ?”"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 24560,
    "dDurationMs": 1040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "no i dont"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 25600,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you didn't know, Destin from smarter every day loves laminar flow,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 30080,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where all the particles of the fluid move parallel to each other in organized layers or laminae"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 35600,
    "dDurationMs": 1640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "look at that it made a bubble!!!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 37240,
    "dDurationMs": 1720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": " "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 38960,
    "dDurationMs": 3880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Where I live people will roll down the window in their car when they see me in the street"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 42920,
    "dDurationMs": 2600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and they will scream “turbulent flow” to me"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 45520,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That happens, that happens in Huntsville. Yeah."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 48560,
    "dDurationMs": 1880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Here- Here's my argument to you, Destin"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 50440,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "nashe"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 54640,
    "dDurationMs": 400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Okay."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 55040,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but turbulent flow if you make that effort is actually more awesome."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 60800,
    "dDurationMs": 940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Um..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 61940,
    "dDurationMs": 1180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "no."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 63120,
    "dDurationMs": 3320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Turbulent flow is not better than laminar. It is awesome"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 66440,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But it is not better than laminar flow."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 69360,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Can I just say I get it"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 70800,
    "dDurationMs": 1560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I get where Destin is coming from"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 72360,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I mean laminar flow is pretty and it's well behaved,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 76120,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Meanwhile turbulent flow is a mess in more ways than one."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 80840,
    "dDurationMs": 5380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I mean, there isn't even a universally agreed-upon definition of turbulent flow."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 86220,
    "dDurationMs": 1360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You know it when you see it"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 87580,
    "dDurationMs": 720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "[Laughing]"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 88440,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Hahaha, So that's the deal with turbulence, you know it when you see it?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 90520,
    "dDurationMs": 1080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Pretty much. Yeah."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 91600,
    "dDurationMs": 3320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So instead of a formal definition, in this video"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 94920,
    "dDurationMs": 4520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we are going to build a checklist of characteristics of turbulent flow,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 99440,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so that you know it when you see it"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 101440,
    "dDurationMs": 5080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the first characteristic of turbulent flow is that it is unpredictable"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 106520,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's right. Turbulent flow is messy it's unpredictable."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 109560,
    "dDurationMs": 3160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It is literally definitionally chaotic"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 112720,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "meaning it is sensitively dependent on initial conditions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 116160,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So if you were to change something somewhere in the fluid"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 119280,
    "dDurationMs": 3080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "well, it would completely change the final state"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 122960,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and that means you can't make predictions with turbulent flow"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 126560,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "All you can do is speak about it statistically."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 129520,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I mean, there are the Navier-Stokes equations which are meant to govern all fluid flow"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 133920,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Including turbulence, but they are notoriously difficult to solve."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 138800,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In fact, there is a million-dollar prize"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 141520,
    "dDurationMs": 7480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for anyone who can even make progress towards getting insight into these equations that would explain turbulence,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 149000,
    "dDurationMs": 2360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so yeah, I get it, turbulence is a mess，"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 151360,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "laminar flow is easy to love"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 153520,
    "dDurationMs": 1640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's like the bell of a ball"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 155160,
    "dDurationMs": 3160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "whereas turbulent flow is kind of an ugly duckling"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 158320,
    "dDurationMs": 5480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But in this video I want to transform that ugly duckling into a beautiful swan"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 163800,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I want you to see that if you make the effort"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 166520,
    "dDurationMs": 8080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The love you can have for turbulent flow is so much deeper and richer than that superficial fling you have with laminar flow"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 178380,
    "dDurationMs": 5540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You are looking at the motion of air in a room, which is generally turbulent"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 183920,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the physics girl and friends imaged a cross-section of air using a fog machine and a laser sheet"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 190080,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "one of the defining characteristics of turbulent flow is that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 193040,
    "dDurationMs": 6360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it consists of many interacting swirls of fluid also called Eddies or Vortices"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 199400,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These eddies span a huge range of sizes"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 203080,
    "dDurationMs": 6320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In the case of air in a room, from the micrometer scale all the way up to meters in diameter"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 209400,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Can you think of another physical phenomenon that exhibits structures over such a range of sizes?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 216000,
    "dDurationMs": 2600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But turbulence can be much larger."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 218720,
    "dDurationMs": 6800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The surface of the Sun is turbulent as hot plasma rises to the surface in huge convection currents."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 225520,
    "dDurationMs": 4280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The cell like structures here are roughly the size of Texas"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 229800,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Larger still are the turbulent swirls on Jupiter."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 233000,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The Great Red Spot is a vortex bigger than the Earth"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 236920,
    "dDurationMs": 3400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The rest of the planet is covered in Eddie's of all sizes"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 240340,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "down to the limits of our ability to measure them from orbiting spacecraft"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 245480,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Even the dust between the stars is in turbulent motion"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 250520,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It makes radio sources twinkle the same way the turbulence in our atmosphere makes stars twinkle"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 256360,
    "dDurationMs": 6800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a stunning example of this turbulent dust is the Orion Nebula: twenty four light years across"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 263720,
    "dDurationMs": 6360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Turbulence is cosmic. In contrast, laminar flow has to be small."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 271000,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This was shown experimentally in 1883."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 274200,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Osborne Reynolds passed water through a glass pipe at different flow rates"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 278400,
    "dDurationMs": 4680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and to visualize the flow, he introduced a stream of dye in the middle of the pipe"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 283080,
    "dDurationMs": 4920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He found at low flow rates the dye remained in a steady stream: laminar flow"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 288000,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but as the flow rate increased the dye began to oscillate back and forth"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 292560,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and beyond a certain critical point, the dye became completely diffused throughout the pipe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 298320,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This was turbulent flow."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 301200,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Reynolds had observed another essential characteristic of turbulence,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 304720,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It is diffusive, meaning it mixes things together"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 308920,
    "dDurationMs": 2440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Turbulent flows caused things to spread out"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 311360,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "not only dye, but also heat or momentum"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 314840,
    "dDurationMs": 2840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They all become distributed throughout the fluid"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 318640,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Reynolds found the transition to turbulence was not only dependent on the flow rate"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 322840,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "turbulence occurred more readily in wider pipes"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 326040,
    "dDurationMs": 3640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But less readily with more viscous fluids, things like honey"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 330320,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He calculated a dimensionless quantity now called the Reynolds number"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 334040,
    "dDurationMs": 5800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Equal to the velocity of the fluid times the characteristic length, say the diameter of the pipe"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 339840,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Divided by the kinematic viscosity of the fluid"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 342720,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which you can think of as a measure of its internal friction"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 346880,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "high Reynolds numbers result in turbulent flow"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 351240,
    "dDurationMs": 3560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Have a look at the smoke rising from a candle flame"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 354800,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "At first, it's laminar. But the hot gases accelerate as they rise,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 359440,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and once the Reynolds number gets too big the smoke transitions to turbulence"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 364320,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so laminar flow only occurs at low Reynolds numbers"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 368720,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Which means it is limited to low speeds small sizes or viscous fluids"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 374400,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is why in our everyday lives most fluid flow is turbulent"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 378520,
    "dDurationMs": 1960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Turbulent flow is the rule."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 380480,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Laminar flow is the exception."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 382960,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The air flowing in and out of your lungs is turbulent,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 385720,
    "dDurationMs": 2600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the blood pumping through your aorta is turbulent"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 388320,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the Atmosphere near the surface of the earth is turbulent"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 391680,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as is the air flow in and around cumulus and cumulonimbus clouds"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 396240,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In fact modeling shows that turbulent flow plays an essential role in the formation of rain drops"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 401760,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so turbulence literally makes it rain."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 404640,
    "dDurationMs": 4740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "[Thunder crashes, Rain sounds]"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 409380,
    "dDurationMs": 3380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I'm going to create turbulence in this rheoscopic fluid"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 413400,
    "dDurationMs": 3640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Rheoscopic just means that it shows the currents"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 417040,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and it does that by having these tiny particles suspended in the water"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 421840,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But what you notice if you look at this turbulent flow is that it gradually dies away"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 427280,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And that's because another characteristic of turbulence is that it's dissipative"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 431600,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That is it takes in energy at the largest scales at these big eddies,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 435800,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then that energy gets transferred down to smaller and smaller eddies"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 439920,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "until on the smallest scales that energy gets dissipated to the fluid as heat"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 445440,
    "dDurationMs": 2440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And so in order to maintain turbulence"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 447880,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You need a constant source of energy, something to keep generating those large eddies,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 452840,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which is why we often think about turbulence around objects that move through a fluid"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 457400,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "things like planes cars or boats."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 459960,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So I want to think about the interface between an object and the fluid."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 464440,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So picture fluid flowing over a flat surface"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 468120,
    "dDurationMs": 6560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "far away from the surface, the fluid isn't affected. It keeps moving with what will call its free stream velocity"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 474680,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But right at the surface，due to friction and adhesion"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 478600,
    "dDurationMs": 4920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The molecules of the fluid are effectively stuck to the surface. Their velocity is zero."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 484520,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The fluid next to it can flow only slowly due to friction with this stationary layer"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 490400,
    "dDurationMs": 7080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with increasing distance from the surface，the fluids velocity increases from zero until it reaches the free stream velocity"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 499120,
    "dDurationMs": 4280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and this region of velocity adjustment is known as a boundary layer."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 503880,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In this case, it's a laminar boundary layer"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 507040,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To form this boundary layer, the surface is applying a force to the fluid"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 512040,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That means the fluid is applying an equal and opposite force on the surface"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 517000,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and this is known as skin friction"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 522720,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now if the fluid velocity is particularly fast or if the surface is long"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 526880,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the boundary layer will grow and eventually transition to turbulence"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 531320,
    "dDurationMs": 7920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in a turbulent boundary layer，the fluid swirls and mixes bringing faster flowing fluid closer to the surface"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 539240,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and this increases the skin friction"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 542360,
    "dDurationMs": 4840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so turbulent boundary layers result in significantly more drag than laminar ones"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 547800,
    "dDurationMs": 4280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the boundary layers around planes and large ships are mostly turbulent"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 552080,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and skin friction accounts for the majority of the drag they experience"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 556360,
    "dDurationMs": 7840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to make matters worse laminar boundary layers can be tripped into becoming turbulent by small obstacles or rough surfaces"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 564200,
    "dDurationMs": 6120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in practice this means clean smooth surfaces can significantly reduce drag saving on fuel costs"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 570320,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If your car is really dirty, it likely gets worse gas mileage than if it were clean"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 575680,
    "dDurationMs": 2360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is what the Mythbusters found when they tested it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 578560,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It also explains why planes are frequently washed"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 583200,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So when you think about airplanes, I imagine that they would be built as smooth as possible"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 589040,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I think of the scene in The Aviator"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 590840,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where Leo says he wants all of the rivets shaved down flush"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 594800,
    "dDurationMs": 6280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and you can see that with this plane all of these screws are are set in to the wing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 601080,
    "dDurationMs": 2600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and really to make the smoothest surface possible,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 603680,
    "dDurationMs": 6880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but then you look over here and there are these ridges that stick up out of the plane,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 610560,
    "dDurationMs": 2200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which seem to make no sense"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 612760,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I mean, why would you add roughness to the surface of the wing?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 616880,
    "dDurationMs": 6920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the answer is actually to induce turbulence in the flow of air over the wing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 623800,
    "dDurationMs": 4440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "when cruising in level flight, air smoothly follows the curve of the wing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 628240,
    "dDurationMs": 4360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but at low speeds or higher angles of attack the airflow can separate"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 632600,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you can think of it as not having enough energy to follow the curve of the wing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 636840,
    "dDurationMs": 4840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This leads to a condition known as stall which dramatically decreases lift"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 642120,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Here you can see the airflow of via strings taped onto the wing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 646120,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and as the plane slows the flow separates"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 649080,
    "dDurationMs": 2360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the strings go wild"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 651440,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This plane has stalled."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 655040,
    "dDurationMs": 7000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The way to delay flow separation and stall is by adding small fins on the wing called vortex generators"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 662040,
    "dDurationMs": 4440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What these vortex generators do, is they actually cause turbulence"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 666480,
    "dDurationMs": 5160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which mixes the faster flowing higher up air down closer to the surface"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 671640,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so you're energizing that fluid flow as it passes over the wing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 675760,
    "dDurationMs": 6440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and because that flow has greater energy it is able to follow the surface of the wing for longer"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 682200,
    "dDurationMs": 2920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That means the air flow remains attached"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 685120,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and if you have attached airflow over the wing then you can maintain lift"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 690000,
    "dDurationMs": 2360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so in the case of airplanes"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 692360,
    "dDurationMs": 4840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You actually need turbulence and you induce more turbulence on the wing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 697200,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in order to fly efficiently and effectively and be able to climb at higher angles of attack."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 704400,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A similar principle is at work with golf balls."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 708200,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The Scott found out about turbulence the hard way"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 710960,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because they started playing with a very smooth golfball"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 714560,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and it wouldn't fly as far as it would once it got sort of dimple nicked and dirty"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 720320,
    "dDurationMs": 3560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you can see why by observing the airflow in a wind tunnel"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 723880,
    "dDurationMs": 4680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with a smooth ball the air forms a laminar boundary layer over its surface"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 728560,
    "dDurationMs": 3080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this leads to low skin friction, which is a good thing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 731640,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But it also means the air flow separates easily"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 735080,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "leaving a large wake of low pressure turbulent air behind the ball"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 739400,
    "dDurationMs": 1720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and that leads to a different form of drag."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 741120,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Is that a pressure difference drag?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 743120,
    "dDurationMs": 1280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's right, that's a pressure drag."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 744400,
    "dDurationMs": 7440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the boundary layer itself has a skin friction drag and then if it separates there's a pressure drag"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 752520,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And if you force that boundary layer to become turbulent"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 756280,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So you have mud or roughness or mix on the golf ball"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 760300,
    "dDurationMs": 5300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then a turbulent boundary like this can get further around the golf ball before it separates"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 765600,
    "dDurationMs": 3320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And so it reduces that wake and reduces that pressure drag."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 768920,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So by reducing the pressure drag to more than your increase in this kind of drag, golf ball travels further"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 774920,
    "dDurationMs": 600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yep!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 775520,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Golfers started carving grooves into their golf balls"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 778520,
    "dDurationMs": 2920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "before the aerodynamics of this was fully understood"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 781440,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And since then dimples have found to work the best for creating a turbulent boundary layer"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 786880,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Dimples are very shallow compared to the diameter of the golf ball, but they have a pretty massive effect"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 792400,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What sort of effect are we talking?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 794080,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Looking at the drag, and we call it drag coefficient"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 797360,
    "dDurationMs": 6760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You see a really big drop almost a factor of two when the boundary layer becomes turbulent."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 804120,
    "dDurationMs": 4520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So having a turbulent boundary layer reduces the size of the turbulent wake"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 809040,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but turbulent wakes themselves are interesting and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 812400,
    "dDurationMs": 4600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "scientists are looking for ways to harness the energy they contain"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 817000,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I came to Caltech to see this experiment"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 819400,
    "dDurationMs": 4360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where the water flows around a cylinder and transitions to turbulence in its wake"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 823760,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The flow is visualized here using a fluorescent dye"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 828160,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You can see how under the right conditions"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 830240,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Vortices are shed by one side of the cylinder, and then the other,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 833760,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "alternating back and forth in a regular pattern"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 837600,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is known as periodic vortex shedding"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 840480,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the pattern it creates downstream is called a von Karman Vortex Street"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 845920,
    "dDurationMs": 6560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These patterns appear all over the place, most spectacularly in images taken from space"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 852480,
    "dDurationMs": 5320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "At this scale, an Island acts as the obstacle that creates the periodic vortex shedding"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 857800,
    "dDurationMs": 4040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the vortex street is made visible by patterns in the clouds"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 861840,
    "dDurationMs": 3320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These patterns can even be seen from ground level"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 866000,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Obviously this phenomenon is not strictly turbulent because it follows a predictable pattern"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 871200,
    "dDurationMs": 3160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but it is part of the transition to turbulence"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 874360,
    "dDurationMs": 5160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and these scientists are looking for ways to harness the energy in these vortex structures"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 879520,
    "dDurationMs": 4680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "One experiment showed that if you put a dead fish in the wake of an object"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 884200,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it will actually swim upstream"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 888200,
    "dDurationMs": 5480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This suggests fish can take advantage of turbulent water to swim more efficiently"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 893680,
    "dDurationMs": 4280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's just one way that animals have adapted to live in a turbulent world"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 898800,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So to sum up, turbulence is everywhere,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 901360,
    "dDurationMs": 5880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it's inside you around you from the smallest scales up to the largest structures in the universe"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 907240,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and it's useful for flying airplanes, forming raindrops,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 910840,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "making golf balls fly further, and helping fish, dead or alive, swim upstream"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 916400,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In contrast, laminar flow is small, superficial, it's a toy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 921920,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's why it's most notable use is in decorative fountains"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 925440,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It appeals to your desire for order, but the world like turbulence is messy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 932280,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's why I personally prefer the richness, the unpredictability of turbulent flow"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 939160,
    "dDurationMs": 2200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "No, but but turbulent flow has its places too."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 941360,
    "dDurationMs": 5240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I'm actually like studying turbulent flow for like my my schooling,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 946600,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Like I'm studying turbulent flow in rocket nozzles. That's a thing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 950600,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So cheating on laminar flow, is what are you doing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 952840,
    "dDurationMs": 5160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Um, no, yes. Yes, maybe, I don't know"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 958000,
    "dDurationMs": 6440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But I wonder you will not get me to say turbulent flow is not awesome and not beautiful, you will not get me to say that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 964440,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So I will concede and I agree with you turbulent flow is awesome. I will agree"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 969560,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "All right. All right."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 971000,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well it's just not as awesome as laminar flow. Let's be honest"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 978360,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Hey, I just wanted to let you know that this video was filmed"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 981720,
    "dDurationMs": 4840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "before the COVID outbreak and before the shelter-in-place guidance was put into effect"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 986560,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now this portion of the video was sponsored by Cottonelle flushable wipes"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 990160,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and since the outbreak they have been working around the clock to get their products back on shelves"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 995200,
    "dDurationMs": 5640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And back when I filmed this video I actually did a little experiment with these wipes to find out how flushable they really are"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1000840,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So let's check that out"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1002640,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So here I have a baby wipe, a paper towel, and a Cottonelle flushable wipe"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1008080,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and I'm gonna submerge all three of these in the fish tank for 30 minutes"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1012880,
    "dDurationMs": 2600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then test how strong they are"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1016280,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Flushable wipes actually became really important to me a couple years ago"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1020000,
    "dDurationMs": 6960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When the main sewer for my building backed up into my condo and flooded the entire downstairs"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1026960,
    "dDurationMs": 6600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the reason was my neighbor was flushing baby wipes down the toilet and that blocked up the whole system"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1033560,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So it was pretty awful."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1035000,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But in fact, this is a thing people do a lot"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1038000,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There was this study from 2016 that found in the US"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1040960,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "60 million baby wipes are purchased every year"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1043680,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and seven million of them end up being flushed down the toilet"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1047360,
    "dDurationMs": 2440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In fact when they looked in the New York City sewer system"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1049800,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They found that 38 percent of the stuff you find in there is actually these baby wipes"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1055960,
    "dDurationMs": 4760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Meanwhile, 14 million flushable wipes are purchased every year and flushed down toilets"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1060720,
    "dDurationMs": 4040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But they make up only 2% of what you find in the sewer system"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1064760,
    "dDurationMs": 6400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So I think it's so important that whatever you throw in the toilet has to be able to break apart so it doesn't clog everything up."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1071160,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Okay, 30 minutes have elapsed and it is time to test the strength of these three wipes"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1076600,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So I'm gonna test their strength with a roll of pennies."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1080320,
    "dDurationMs": 1560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Here we go on the baby wipe"
    } ]
